From 9f3f3df741254f57322f4e6ae1accaf1e823d927 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhengHaoRangay4hub <ZhengHaoRangay4hub@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 14:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] orangepi-zero2: ignore unreliable TF card-detect signal

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific card-detect workaround]

The H616 BROM can load SPL from the TF card even on boards where the PF6
card-detect signal is not asserted.  The legacy sunxi MMC driver then
checks PF6, reports "MMC: no card present", and stops with -ENOMEDIUM
before it can load U-Boot proper from the same card.

Leave the MMC0 card-detect pin empty so the legacy driver attempts card
initialisation directly.  This matches the polling behaviour used when no
card-detect GPIO is configured and keeps the data and clock wiring
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: ZhengHaoRangay4hub <ZhengHaoRangay4hub@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
index bfe1837..427c7ec 100644
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ CONFIG_DRAM_SUN50I_H616_READ_CALIBRATION=y
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUN50I_H616_READ_TRAINING=y
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUN50I_H616_WRITE_TRAINING=y
 CONFIG_MACH_SUN50I_H616=y
-CONFIG_MMC0_CD_PIN="PF6"
+CONFIG_MMC0_CD_PIN=""
 CONFIG_R_I2C_ENABLE=y
 # CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT is not set
 CONFIG_SPL_I2C=y
-- 
